+  </div>
+</header>
+
+<div class="how">
+  <h2>Four rules so this does not sound read</h2>
+  <ul>
+    <li><b>Read each yellow block once, then look away and say it.</b> If you say it slightly differently every take, that is the point. Only the underlined words are worth keeping exact.</li>
+    <li><b>Talk to the screen, not to the notes.</b> You are showing someone something you built. Your eyes should be where their eyes are.</li>
+    <li><b>Land the full stops.</b> The lines are short on purpose. A pause after a short line reads as confidence. Rushing between them reads as reciting.</li>
+    <li><b>Fumble a word and keep going.</b> Nobody re-records a pitch over one word. Stopping is what makes it obvious there was a script.</li>
+  </ul>
+</div>
+
+<div class="setup">
