+        ALLOW.</strong> Not a timeout, not a malformed response, not a rate
+        limit, not a 500, not a missing API key, not a provider that has been
+        switched off entirely. There is no code path in which the absence of a
+        judgement becomes permission to spend someone's money.
+      </p>
